        "pwm_output",
        "led_high"
      ],
      "notes": "Onboard status LED (D1 on both receiver-v0.1.0 and remote-v0.1.0 hardware — a plain 2-lead LED, NOT the WS2812B loosely implied by picolume.com marketing copy), active-high (GPIO25 -> R8 -> LED anode -> cathode -> GND). Confirmed via github.com/picolume/hardware production KiCad netlists (production/netlist.ipc) for both physical PicoLume board designs — identical GPIO25/R8/D1 wiring on both. digital_input dropped to match this repo's established led_high precedent for dedicated onboard LED pins (rpipico, adafruit_feather_scorpio, wiznet_5500_evb_pico); pwm_output kept since arduino-pico's analogWrite() works on any RP2040 GPIO, enabling brightness dimming.\nCheck if available on board"
    },
